{"id": 66, "ts": 1781191312.042363, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 3, "agent": "agent_2", "message": "I appreciate Sofia\u2019s emphasis on Candidate\u202fB\u2019s stress resilience and technical skills, but the lack of any concrete evidence on his decision\u2011making quality or sense of responsibility leaves a critical safety\u2011relevant gap. Likewise, the new input from Anna confirms that we have no specific observations on Candidate\u202fD\u2019s crew\u2011cooperation, professional communication, or operational reliability\u2014areas that are essential for long\u2011haul cockpit dynamics. In contrast, Candidate\u202fC offers clear, documented strengths that directly map to our core criteria: he \u201cmakes correct decisions quickly,\u201d demonstrating high decision quality, and \u201ckeeps calm in a crisis,\u201d confirming strong stress resilience. He also \u201cunderstands complicated technology,\u201d covering technical competence. While C\u2019s communication style and egocentric attitude are concerns, these are comparable to the interpersonal issues noted for B and D, and can be addressed through targeted CRM training. Given that C provides concrete evidence on the most safety\u2011critical dimensions (decision quality, stress resilience, technical competence) whereas D and B have significant unknowns, I now recommend Candidate\u202fC for the long\u2011distance pilot role."}
